{
  "id": "mushrooms-daterra",
  "title": "Mushrooms & Drugs (Daterra)",
  "thumbnail": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81myyTatZ1L._AC_UF894,1000_QL80_.jpg",
  "description": "",
  "content": "<div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><h1><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; border-radius: 6px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; transition: opacity 0.15s; max-width: 100%; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\">🔗</button>Mushrooms / Fungi</h1><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><br></p></div><div><h2 id=\"heading-61\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\">🔗</button>Dream Flake Mushroom</h2><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Drug</em></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:</strong> Feywild</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:</strong> 5 cp per gram/use. 1 gp per ounce (28 uses).</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:</strong> Black fungus. Dried into thin slivers for use.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Species-Specific:</strong></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Gnomes:</strong> Gnomes experience the hallucinations as intensely mechanical — elaborate impossible machines, infinite clockwork, recursive patterns. Most find it fascinating rather than disturbing. Addiction High for Gnomes.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Elves:</strong> Elves who smoke it do not return from the waking dream on schedule — they remain under for twice the normal duration and wake Exhausted (1 level).</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Beasts:</strong> Beasts that consume it become docile and unfocused for the duration — effectively Incapacitated without losing consciousness.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Consuming:</strong></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Placed Between Cheek and Gum:</strong> As Action or Bonus Action, place a sliver. Induces hallucinations and euphoria.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Smoked:</strong> As an Action, smoke the dream flake. User enters an extremely vivid waking dream lasting several hours.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Extended Use:</strong> Permanently blackens the teeth. Bad trips become increasingly common with repeated use.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Used as Poison:</strong> DC 11 Constitution saving throw to resist most effects. Addiction is still rolled at one level lower than normal.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:</strong> Medium</p></li></ul><div style=\"max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><br style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></div></div><h2 id=\"heading-12\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Trillimac Mushroom.</h2><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:&nbsp;</strong>Underdark.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:&nbsp;</strong>~4 gp per foot of stalk as food (a 4-ft stalk = ~16 gp in food value). Cap material worth 2–5 gp per sheet to cartographers, scribes, and hatmakers.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:&nbsp;</strong>4–5 ft tall cultivated, 3 ft wild. Light gray stalk, broad flat gray-green cap 14–33 inches across. Leathery cap surface.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Lore:&nbsp;</strong>Trillimac caps are the primary writing material of the Underdark — the equivalent of surface parchment. Maps, contracts, spell scrolls, and records scratched on trillimac are common throughout Underdark settlements. A document on trillimac is definitively from the Underdark.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Food — Stalk:&nbsp;</strong>Cleaned, soaked in water 1 hour, dried by fire = bread-like food. 1d6+4 pounds per stalk. 1 lb = 1 ration.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Material — Cap:&nbsp;</strong>Cut and cleaned cap = leathery writing surface. Takes dyes and inks well. Functions as parchment, scroll material, or map material. One cap yields 2–4 usable sheets depending on size. Lasts years if kept dry.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Crafting — Scroll Blank:&nbsp;</strong>Cleaned trillimac cap sheet + any ink, no proficiency required (1 hr during a Rest, no roll required) = a functional scroll blank. Scribing spells onto trillimac follows normal scroll crafting rules but costs nothing for the paper/parchment component.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Crafting — Underdark Map:&nbsp;</strong>Trillimac sheet + ormu ink or any pigment, Cartographer's Tools and proficiency (1 hr during a Rest, no roll needed) = a durable map that survives moisture, heat, and rough handling better than paper.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Crafting — Trillimac Hat:&nbsp;</strong>A fresh, large cap shaped while damp and dried to form (no tools, DC 10 Dexterity, 1 hr during a Rest) = a functional wide-brimmed hat.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction: None</strong></p></li></ul></div><div><br></div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-14\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Zurkhwood Mushroom</h2><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:&nbsp;</strong>Underdark. Widely cultivated by nearly every Underdark race.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value — Lumber:&nbsp;</strong>5–15 gp per cut plank depending on quality and grain pattern.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value — Spores (food):&nbsp;</strong>1–2 sp per pound of food.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:&nbsp;</strong>30–40 ft tall. Tree-like in silhouette. Hard, woody stalks with distinctive internal grain patterns revealed by cutting.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Lore:&nbsp;</strong>Zurkhwood is the oak of the Underdark. Every surface material made from wood has an Underdark equivalent made from zurkhwood — furniture, barrels, doors, wagon beds, weapon hafts, bowls, coffins, bridges, and boats.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Food :&nbsp;</strong>grain-like, yields 1d4+4 pounds of food per specimen. Ground up, baked into rough bread, or eaten raw. Bland but nutritious.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Material — Lumber:&nbsp;</strong>Functions identically to hardwood for any crafting purpose. HP and AC of zurkhwood objects = treated as hardwood (AC 5, 10 HP per inch of thickness). Floats in water.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Crafting — Zurkhwood Raft:&nbsp;</strong>3 cut zurkhwood stalks + rope or vine binding, Carpenter's Tools and proficiency (DC12 roll only needed if no proficiency) = a functional raft carrying up to 4 Medium creatures and gear. Takes 4 hours to build. Floats indefinitely. Essential for Darklake travel.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction: None</strong></p></li></ul><div><font color=\"#c2ac83\"><b><br></b></font></div><div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-18\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Timmask Mushroom.</h2><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:&nbsp;</strong>Underdark</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:&nbsp;</strong>150 gp per sealed vial of ground powder (enough for 5 uses).</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:&nbsp;</strong>Squat 2-ft toadstool, beige cap with vivid red and orange stripes. Smells foul.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Lore:&nbsp;</strong>Tanar'ri demons consider timmask a delicacy — one of very few material-world substances they actively desire to eat.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Species-Specific:</strong></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Demons:&nbsp;</strong>Recognize the smell instantly and are drawn to it. A creature holding or offering an intact timmask gets one round of pause before a demon acts aggressively — useful in negotiation or as a distraction.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Harvesting:&nbsp;</strong>Uprooting, heavy damage, or destruction triggers a Spore Cloud: 15-ft-radius cloud of poisonous spores. Creatures in the area make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned. While poisoned this way, the creature is affected as though by a<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Confusion</em>spell for 1 minute. When the effect ends, the poisoned condition ends with it.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Effect — Demon Summoning:&nbsp;</strong>An intact timmask offered during a demon summoning ritual grants advantage on the summoning check and increases the likelihood a demon responds without immediate hostility.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Crafting — Spore Vial:&nbsp;</strong>1hr during a Rest. DC 17 Nature, Survival, or Medicine check; proficiency required. On success, yields one sealed vial of timmask spores. Thrown (range 20 ft): triggers a Spore Cloud on impact (see When Harvesting).</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Effect — Necromancy Spell Components:&nbsp;</strong>Ground timmask powder used as an additional spell component doubles the duration of Necromancy spells (where applicable) and adds +1 damage per die to damage rolls.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:&nbsp;</strong>None</p></li></ul><div><br></div></div><div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-19\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Tongue of Madness Mushroom.</h2><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:&nbsp;</strong>Underdark</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:&nbsp;</strong>9 gp per specimen</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:&nbsp;</strong>Long, slender mushroom resembling an oversized human tongue. Named for both its shape and what it does to yours.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Lore:&nbsp;</strong>Named for both its appearance and its effect — a creature that eats one cannot keep a thought to itself.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Species-Specific:</strong></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Drow:&nbsp;</strong>Drow use it in interrogation as a confession accelerant — a subject who cannot stop vocalizing their thoughts requires no other persuasion.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Crafting — Honesty Wine:&nbsp;</strong>Tongue of Madness steeped in wine for 24 hrs + any fruit or sweetener, Cook's Tools and proficiency (no roll needed) = one bottle of wine that functions as Tongue of Madness per glass. Each glass requires a DC 10 Con save instead of DC 12, making it easy to administer casually across multiple servings.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Food:&nbsp;</strong>Edible. Counts as 1 ration. Tastes unremarkable for something so dramatic in effect.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Consuming:&nbsp;</strong>Action or Bonus Action, consume the mushroom. DC 12 Constitution saving throw or compulsively speak every thought aloud for 1 hour. This ends Concentration.<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Lesser restoration</em>or similar ends the effect early.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:&nbsp;</strong>Low</p></li></ul></div><div><br></div><div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-21\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Bigwig (Faerzress-Suffused Fungi)</h2><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:&nbsp;</strong>Underdark</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:&nbsp;</strong>50–100 gp each</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:&nbsp;</strong>4 inches tall, thin stem, wide purple cap.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Food:&nbsp;</strong>Counts as 1 ration.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Consuming:</strong></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Enlarge:&nbsp;</strong>DC 12 Constitution saving throw (you may choose to fail). On a failed save, you double in size and weigh 8x as much, functioning as the<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Enlarge</em>effect from<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Enlarge/Reduce</em>for 1 hour.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Extend:&nbsp;</strong>Each additional bigwig consumed extends the duration by 1 hour. Size does not stack — only duration.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Tingling Warning:</strong>10 minutes before the effect expires, you feel a tingle, prompting you to eat another or prepare to return to normal size.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Cancelled By:&nbsp;</strong>Eating a pygmywort, or any magical<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Reduce</em>effect.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">While Enlarged:&nbsp;</strong>+1d4 damage on melee attacks (as the<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Enlarge</em>spell), advantage on Strength checks and saving throws, disadvantage on Stealth checks. Cannot fit through standard doorways.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:&nbsp;</strong>None</p></li></ul><div><br></div><h2 id=\"heading-22\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\">🔗</button>Pygmywort (Faerzress-Suffused Fungi)</h2><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:&nbsp;</strong>Underdark</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:&nbsp;</strong>50–100 gp each</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:&nbsp;</strong>1 inch tall, short stem, stubby blue cap with white dots.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Food:&nbsp;</strong>Edible. Counts as 1 ration.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Consuming:&nbsp;</strong>Action or Bonus Action, consume the mushroom.</p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Reduce:&nbsp;</strong>DC 12 Constitution saving throw (you may choose to fail). On a failed save, you halve in size and weigh 1/8 as much, functioning as the<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Reduce</em>effect from<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Enlarge/Reduce</em>for 1 hour.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Extend:&nbsp;</strong>Each additional pygmywort consumed extends the duration by 1 hour. Same tingling warning mechanic as bigwig.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Cancelled By:&nbsp;</strong>Eating a bigwig, or any magical<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Enlarge</em>effect.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">While Reduced:&nbsp;</strong>+1 AC, advantage on Stealth checks, −1d4 damage on melee attacks (as the<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Reduce</em>spell). Can fit through any space a Tiny creature could pass through.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:&nbsp;</strong>None</p></li></ul></div><div><br></div><div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-58\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Angel's Trumpet Mushroom</h2><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Drug</em></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:</strong>&nbsp;Feywild, Material Plane (Surface), Underdark</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:</strong>&nbsp;10–100 gp depending on potency</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Effects — Burned &amp; Inhaled:</strong>&nbsp;As an Action, burn and inhale the mushroom. Unwilling creatures make a DC 11 Constitution saving throw to resist inhalation.</p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\">On inhalation: take 1d4 psychic damage.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\">The creature then begins seeing and conversing with dead relatives, friends, or others who died nearby — casually, without distress or confusion.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\">Visions are intermittent: roll 1d10 for total number of instances. For each, roll 1d12 to determine hours before the next instance. Each instance lasts 1d6 hours.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:</strong>&nbsp;None</p></li></ul><div><br></div></div><div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-66\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Kammarth Mushroom</h2><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Drug</em></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:</strong>&nbsp;Underdark</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:</strong>&nbsp;80 gp</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:</strong>&nbsp;Sold as a powder or beige-colored jelly. Taken orally or through skin contact.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Consuming:</strong>&nbsp;As an Action or Bonus Action, consume the mushroom orally or apply through skin contact.</p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Effect:</strong>&nbsp;You feel boundless energy and well-being. You act as if under&nbsp;<em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Expeditious Retreat</em>&nbsp;spell and gain advantage on all Dexterity checks for 1d4 minutes.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Two Doses within 8 Hours:</strong>&nbsp;Take 1d6 psychic damage and become Paralyzed for 1d6 minutes.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Three or More Doses within 24 Hours:</strong>&nbsp;Take 6d6 psychic damage and become Paralyzed for 1d6 hours.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Used as Poison:</strong>&nbsp;DC 12 Constitution saving throw to resist most effects. Addiction is still rolled at one level lower than normal.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:</strong>&nbsp;Medium</p></li></ul></div><div><br></div><div><!--StartFragment--><h2 id=\"heading-56\" style=\"margin: 18px 0px 8px; color: rgb(211, 154, 57); max-width: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;\"><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\"><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">🔗</button>Ziran / \"Bloodfast\" Mushroom</h2><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><em style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Drug (Drow)</em></p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Found In:</strong>&nbsp;Underdark, Material Plane (Surface). Originally exclusively a Drow refinement of certain mushrooms, but the secret has reached the surface and some alchemists have begun cultivating the necessary mushrooms.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Value:</strong>&nbsp;100 gp</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Appearance:</strong>&nbsp;Bitter white powder refined from several Underdark fungi by the Drow.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Lore:</strong>&nbsp;Originally a Drow refinement, the method has reached the surface and some alchemists have begun cultivating the necessary fungi independently.</p></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">When Consuming:</strong>&nbsp;As an Action or Bonus Action, consume the powder. You are Stunned for 1 round, then gain +2 Dexterity for 1d3 hours. Afterward, you suffer one level of Exhaustion, take 1d6 psychic damage, and experience a sense of detachment — feeling as if watching yourself act from a distance.</p><ul data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Used as Poison:</strong>&nbsp;DC 13 Constitution saving throw to resist most effects. Addiction is still rolled at one level lower than normal.</p></li></ul></li><li data-label=\"•\" data-list-type=\"bullet\" data-spread=\"false\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><strong style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Addiction:</strong>&nbsp;High</p></li></ul></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><h1><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\">🔗</button>Drugs (non-mushroom)</h1><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><br></p></div><div><h2><button class=\"heading-anchor-btn\" title=\"Copy link to this section\" style=\"margin: 0px 0.3em 0px -1.4em; max-width: 100%; background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; transition: opacity 0.15s; padding: 0px 2px !important; font-size: 0.55em !important;\">🔗</button>Yggdrasil Sap</h2><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><i style=\"max-width: 100%;\">Drug (anywhere)</i></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\">10,000gp per use.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\">A legendary, very rare, and powerful drug that lets users see their future, often showing them their own death. However, using it is extremely risky — if the user does not pass a DC 15 Constitution save, they die from the drug's effects.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\">Not addictive.</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; max-width: 100%; width: auto !important; min-width: 0px !important;\"><br style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></p></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>",
